course: dictionary
lesson: 12727
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, read the words around it. «We played draughts after tea.» The word played tells you draughts is a game here, not a breeze or a drink.
explain: Draughts can also mean cold air coming in through gaps. «Keep out the draughts» means stop the cold air getting into the room. The word keep and the idea of cold help you see this meaning.
explain: Draughts can mean a long swallow of a drink too. «He took long draughts of cold lemonade on the hot day.» The word lemonade and the words long swallow fit the drink meaning.
fact: Draughts is a board game for two players. Each player moves flat pieces diagonally.
fact: In the USA, draughts is called checkers.
fact: A draught is a cold current of air that comes through gaps, such as under a door or round a window.
fact: Draughts can also mean long swallows of a drink.
fact: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. Does «a game of draughts» make sense? Yes, so the game meaning fits.
exercise: «We played draughts after tea, moving our flat pieces diagonally.» What is draughts here? | A cold wind through a gap | * A board game for two players | A long swallow of juice | A kind of fish
exercise: «Put a rolled towel at the bottom of the door to stop the draughts.» What are the draughts? | Birds flying into the room | A game with flat pieces | * Cold currents of air coming through gaps | Loud noises from the kitchen
exercise: «He took long draughts of cold lemonade on the hot day.» What does draughts mean here? | * Long swallows of a drink | Cold air moving in a room | Games played on a board | Small wooden pieces
test: In the USA, what is draughts called? | * Checkers | Chess | Snakes | Ludo
test: «Jess felt a cold draught by the window.» What is a draught? | * A current of cold air | A type of board | A game for two players | A long drink
exam: Which meaning of draughts fits best in «Ben and Sam sat down to a game of draughts»? | A sort of bread | A long swallow | A cold air current | * A board game for two players
